  "summary": "Malicious code in agentic-awesome-skills (npm)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (bce718f3dabec30c962c7aecf6eb41f2583d7158f48af6dca9ec8adac61f6297)\nPackage ships a large collection of 'skills' subdirectories (8234 files scanned), each containing its own helper scripts. Static patterns matched on keyword co-occurrence: Python scrapers using GET/POST and ping (skills/junta-leiloeiros/scripts/scraper/base_scraper.py, serve_api.py), a benchmark runner script (skills/loki-mode/benchmarks/run-benchmarks.sh) containing curl invocations and an 'install' token, an rclone installer helper that fetches from the official rclone.org domain (skills/rclone-cli/scripts/install.sh line 15: curl https://rclone.org), and a youtube-notetaker verify.sh issuing curl GETs. The matched destinations are either the project's own official domain (rclone.org) or generic verb/keyword co-occurrence in domain-specific tooling; no hardcoded attacker C2, no browser/credential store enumeration, no shipped third-party credentials, no wallet/seed scanning, and no evidence of install-time fetch-and-execute from an anonymous or author-mutable host were observed in the matched excerpts. The scripts are not wired to npm lifecycle hooks that would auto-run on install of the npm package itself.\n\n## Source: ghsa-malware (9e6f2f16354be2dc09e9b3f437c66f13fbe8ea2abed07f5d4bf8281e2ffeebb2)\nAny computer that has this package installed or running should be considered fully compromised. All secrets and keys stored on that computer should be rotated immediately from a different computer. The package should be removed, but as full control of the computer may have been given to an outside entity, there is no guarantee that removing the package will remove all malicious software resulting from installing it.\n",
